									"numinlets" : 1,
									"numoutlets" : 0,
									"patching_rect" : [ 42.0, 66.0, 429.0, 275.0 ],
									"text" : "I have compiled as much information as possible for the various venues and rehearsal spaces of the Korean Electronic Music Festival. The speaker positions are presented here in SPAT5 format. (free to download from www.ircam.fr).  I am also making use of the CNMAT Odot Package (available in the Max Package Manager). \n\nEach of the tabs illustrate the speaker layouts for the various spaces. No participant should feel obligated to use the full complement of speakers in any venue, but this document should show you what is possible in each of the spaces. In fact, if we try to use all of the speakers in each of the venues, we may invite additional technical complications. As always, the best advice I can offer is to make things as simple as possible...but not simpler.\n\nPlease reach out to me with any questions.\n\nKind regards,\n\nJeremy Wagner\nTechnical Director, CNMAT\njeremy.wagner@berkeley.edu"
								}

							}
